# Noisecore

A responsive e-commerce website prototype for a fictional audio technology brand.

## Live Demo

[Noisecore Website](https://brianfil.github.io/noisecore-website/)

## About

Noisecore is a front-end web development project built to practice creating a responsive e-commerce website using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

The website includes product pages, promotional sections, navigation, and responsive layouts for desktop and mobile devices.

## Features

- Responsive design
- Product showcase
- Product pages
- Promotional deals section
- Responsive navigation
- Interactive elements
- Desktop and mobile layouts

## Technologies

- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript

## Project Structure

```text
Noisecore/
├── asset/
├── asset2/
├── css/
├── html/
├── js/
└── productasset/
```

## Running the Project

No dependencies are required.

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Brianfil/noisecore-website.git
```

Then open:

```text
Noisecore/html/index.html
```

in a web browser.

